# 🆔 AETHERIA — ID SYSTEM

> **Everything that exists in Aetheria must have an identity.**
>
> The ID System provides a unique identity for every persistent entity in the game.
>
> Every registered ID can be stored, retrieved, updated, and referenced through the **Database System**.

---

# 📌 1. OVERVIEW

The **ID System** is responsible for generating, assigning, validating, and managing unique identifiers for entities within Aetheria.

The system is used by:

```text
Master
Character
NPC
Enemy
Item
```

and can later be expanded to:

```text
Faction
Location
Quest
Event
Dungeon
Floor
Party
Equipment
Skill
Story
World
```

The fundamental relationship is:

```text
ENTITY
   ↓
ID SYSTEM
   ↓
UNIQUE ID
   ↓
DATABASE SYSTEM
   ↓
PERSISTENT DATA
```

---

# 🎯 2. PURPOSE

The ID System exists to prevent ambiguity between entities.

For example, multiple characters can have the same display name:

```text
Alex
Alex
Alex
```

Their identities remain different:

```text
CHAR_000001
CHAR_000145
CHAR_000872
```

Therefore:

> **Name is not identity.**

The ID is the permanent identity of the entity.

---

# 🧠 3. CORE PRINCIPLE

Every persistent entity must have a unique ID.

```text
MASTER_000001
CHAR_000001
NPC_000001
ENEMY_000001
ITEM_000001
```

The ID should remain stable even when the entity changes.

For example:

```text
CHAR_000001

Name:
Arden

Level:
10
```

Later:

```text
CHAR_000001

Name:
Arden

Level:
50
```

The ID remains:

```text
CHAR_000001
```

---

# 🏗️ 4. ID SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE

```text
                         ID SYSTEM
                            │
             ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
             │              │              │
             ▼              ▼              ▼
         GENERATOR      VALIDATOR       REGISTRY
             │              │              │
             └──────────────┼──────────────┘
                            │
                            ▼
                       UNIQUE ID
                            │
                            ▼
                     DATABASE SYSTEM
```

The ID System generates and validates identity.

The Database System stores the entity associated with that identity.

