# 🧩 11. ENTITY ID VS INSTANCE ID

Aetheria should distinguish between an **Entity Definition ID** and an **Entity Instance ID** when necessary.

Example:

```text
ENEMY TYPE

ENEMY_TYPE_CORRUPTED_KNIGHT
```

This defines what the enemy is.

An individual spawned enemy can then have:

```text
ENEMY_000451
```

Therefore:

```text
ENEMY TYPE
     │
     ▼
Corrupted Knight
     │
     ├── ENEMY_000451
     ├── ENEMY_000452
     └── ENEMY_000453
```

This distinction is useful for procedural enemies.

The same principle can apply to:

```text
Character Template
NPC Template
Item Definition
Enemy Template
```

