# 🔢 14. UNIQUE ID RULE

An ID must never be duplicated within the same entity namespace.

Valid:

```text
CHAR_000001
CHAR_000002
CHAR_000003
```

Invalid:

```text
CHAR_000001
CHAR_000001
```

Different entity types can have the same numeric sequence.

For example:

```text
CHAR_000001
NPC_000001
ITEM_000001
```

are valid because their prefixes define different namespaces.

---

# 🔒 15. ID IMMUTABILITY

Once an ID has been assigned, it should normally never change.

Example:

```text
CHAR_000001
```

The following may change:

```text
Name
Level
Class
Star
Faction
Location
Equipment
Relationship
Status
```

But:

```text
CharacterID
```

remains unchanged.

This ensures that database references remain valid.

---

# 🗄️ 16. DATABASE RELATIONSHIP

Every ID is stored in the Database System.

Example:

```text
ID SYSTEM
    │
    ▼
CHAR_000001
    │
    ▼
DATABASE
    │
    └── Character Data
```

The database can then retrieve:

```text
CHAR_000001
```

and return its complete state.

