# 🗑️ 27. DELETE RULE

An ID should generally not be reused after deletion.

Example:

```text
CHAR_000125
```

Character dies permanently.

The record may become:

```text
Status:
DEAD
```

rather than physically deleting the database record.

If the record must be deleted:

```text
CHAR_000125
```

should remain reserved.

The next character becomes:

```text
CHAR_000126
```

not:

```text
CHAR_000125
```

This prevents historical references from becoming ambiguous.

---

# 💀 28. DEATH AND PERSISTENCE

Important entities should retain their IDs after death.

Example:

```text
CHAR_000125
Status:
DEAD
```

This allows the game to remember:

```text
Character died
Character's quests
Character relationships
Character history
Character achievements
Character involvement in events
```

The same principle applies to:

```text
NPC
Enemy
Faction
Boss
```

where persistent history is required.

