# ✨ 42. FINAL PRINCIPLE

Aetheria follows this rule:

> **Every important entity has an identity.**

```text
MASTER
CHARACTER
NPC
ENEMY
ITEM
```

Each receives a unique ID.

```text
MASTER_000001
CHAR_000001
NPC_000001
ENEMY_000001
ITEM_000001
```

The Game State System controls the state of those entities.

The Database System stores those states.

The ID System connects everything.

Therefore:

```text
CORE WORLD
     ↓
GAME MANAGER
     ↓
GAME STATE SYSTEM
     ↓
ENTITY
     ↓
ID SYSTEM
     ↓
DATABASE SYSTEM
     ↓
PERSISTENT MEMORY
```

> **The ID identifies the entity.**
>
> **The Game State defines its current condition.**
>
> **The Database remembers it.**

This creates the foundation for a persistent Aetheria where a character, NPC, enemy, or item can be individually tracked throughout the entire history of the world.
